{
  "_comment": "The amplification counts: each writer the engine tallies, and each half of the table-read count and the wrapper that feeds it, left out in turn. tests/test_stats.cpp checks the engine's counts of what it wrote and what it read against the simulated disk's counts of what was appended and what was served, by kind of file, so a counter that stops moving is a mismatch rather than a smaller number nobody questions. The per-level split in ambar.stats is the same counters again by level and is not checked separately.",

  "log: count the record's payload and not its header": [
    "src/wal.cpp",
    "  bytes_written_ += kHeaderSize + length;",
    "  bytes_written_ += length;"
  ],
  "log: leave the padding at a block's end uncounted": [
    "src/wal.cpp",
    "        bytes_written_ += block_left;",
    "        ;"
  ],
  "flush: leave the table uncounted": [
    "src/db_impl.cpp",
    "    flush_bytes_ += meta.file_size;",
    "    ;"
  ],
  "compaction: leave the outputs uncounted": [
    "src/db_impl.cpp",
    "    compaction_bytes_ += compact->total_bytes;",
    "    ;"
  ],
  "manifest: leave a new database's first manifest uncounted": [
    "src/db_impl.cpp",
    "    versions_->add_manifest_bytes(log.bytes_written());",
    "    ;"
  ],
  "manifest: leave the edits after open uncounted": [
    "src/version_set.cpp",
    "    manifest_bytes_ += descriptor_log_->bytes_written() - manifest_before;",
    "    (void)manifest_before;"
  ],
  "table reads: leave the count unmoved": [
